event: text_delta
data: {"delta": "To store harvested maize properly and"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": " prevent loss from dampness or pests like the grain borer:\n\n1. **Dry the maize properly**: Ensure the"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": " grain moisture content is reduced to **12-13%** (a grain should crack cleanly when bitten). Dry"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": " on clean tarpaulins off the bare soil.\n2. **Shell and clean**: Remove broken grains, cob debris"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": ", and dust, as trash attracts insects.\n3. **Use hermetic storage bags**: Store the cleaned grains in airtight"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": " hermetic bags (such as PICS bags) without applying chemicals, or treat with approved storage dust (like Actell"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": "ic Super at **50 g per 90 kg bag**) if using standard jute or woven polypropylene bags.\n4"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": ". **Stack off the floor**: Store sealed bags on wooden pallets in a cool, well-ventilated room at least **3"}

event: text_delta
data: {"delta": "0 cm** away from walls.\n\n\n"}

